        <div><a name="_manchu" id="_manchu"></a><p class="h2Annex">C.30 Manchu</p><p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_a6b9b1d0-cdc6-4b40-a85b-55bb6d6b088b" id="_a6b9b1d0-cdc6-4b40-a85b-55bb6d6b088b"></a>name components:</p>

  <p style="mso-list:l3 level1 lfo32;" class="MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst">
    family name
  </p>
  <p style="mso-list:l3 level1 lfo32;" class="MsoListParagraphCxSpLast">
    given name
  </p>

<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_940bc532-df45-42eb-bd10-3ef1f7974281" id="_940bc532-df45-42eb-bd10-3ef1f7974281"></a>Manchus are called only by their given names.
Manchu clan names (&#x201C;hala&#x201D;) are not used with their personal names,
but occasionally a family name is used.</p>
<div><a name="_typical_name_patterns_10" id="_typical_name_patterns_10"></a><p class="h3Annex">C.30.1 Typical name patterns</p><p class="TableTitle" align="center">Table C.40</p><div align="center"><table style="mso-table-lspace:15.0cm;margin-left:423.0pt;mso-table-rspace:15.0cm;margin-right:423.0pt;mso-table-bspace:14.2pt;mso-table-anchor-vertical:paragraph;mso-table-anchor-horizontal:column;mso-table-overlap:never;" class="MsoISOTable" border="1" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0"><a name="_1a9a73dc-5050-4add-8070-5195767a72c7" id="_1a9a73dc-5050-4add-8070-5195767a72c7"></a><tbody><tr><td align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;">given name</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<p class="TableTitle" align="center">Table C.41</p><div align="center"><table style="mso-table-lspace:15.0cm;margin-left:423.0pt;mso-table-rspace:15.0cm;margin-right:423.0pt;mso-table-bspace:14.2pt;mso-table-anchor-vertical:paragraph;mso-table-anchor-horizontal:column;mso-table-overlap:never;" class="MsoISOTable" border="1" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0"><a name="_08fca61a-383f-42e9-b9a2-d9752e4eb7d9" id="_08fca61a-383f-42e9-b9a2-d9752e4eb7d9"></a><tbody><tr><td align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;">given name</td><td align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;">family name</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<p class="TableTitle" align="center">Table C.42</p><div align="center"><table style="mso-table-lspace:15.0cm;margin-left:423.0pt;mso-table-rspace:15.0cm;margin-right:423.0pt;mso-table-bspace:14.2pt;mso-table-anchor-vertical:paragraph;mso-table-anchor-horizontal:column;mso-table-overlap:never;" class="MsoISOTable" border="1" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0"><a name="_09f55db8-aa59-4bef-877a-76f8aa9109d7" id="_09f55db8-aa59-4bef-877a-76f8aa9109d7"></a><tbody><tr><td align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;">family name</td><td align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;">given name</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>
<div><a name="_examples_10" id="_examples_10"></a><p class="h3Annex">C.30.2 Examples</p><div class="example"><a name="_94aba685-4b5e-4722-b486-70015b53c5c2" id="_94aba685-4b5e-4722-b486-70015b53c5c2"></a><p class="MsoNormal"><span class="example_label">EXAMPLE  1</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>&#x201C;Tuli&#x161;en&#x201D;</p></div>
<div class="example"><a name="_fe859e09-0165-45b3-8808-d576b62103a5" id="_fe859e09-0165-45b3-8808-d576b62103a5"></a><p class="MsoNormal"><span class="example_label">EXAMPLE  2</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>&#x201C;Hiowan Ye&#x201D; (&#x7384;&#x70E8;)</p></div>
<div class="example"><a name="_c50f3025-b123-448d-9311-4856f761bff4" id="_c50f3025-b123-448d-9311-4856f761bff4"></a><p class="MsoNormal"><span class="example_label">EXAMPLE  3</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>&#x201C;Aisin-Gioro Ulhicun&#x201D;, linguist. The family name is &#x201C;Aisin-Gioro&#x201D;.</p></div></div></div>
        <div><a name="_mongolian" id="_mongolian"></a><p class="h2Annex">C.31 Mongolian</p><p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_2bc4203e-9c32-4c97-8590-1c9d374ab5c2" id="_2bc4203e-9c32-4c97-8590-1c9d374ab5c2"></a>name components:</p>

  <p style="mso-list:l3 level1 lfo33;" class="MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst">
    given name
  </p>
  <p style="mso-list:l3 level1 lfo33;" class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle">
    clan name
  </p>
  <p style="mso-list:l3 level1 lfo33;" class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle">
    family name
  </p>
  <p style="mso-list:l3 level1 lfo33;" class="MsoListParagraphCxSpLast">
    genonymic name
  </p>

<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_2bcaa041-1a93-4b6a-a9c3-8b382f3f3dd3" id="_2bcaa041-1a93-4b6a-a9c3-8b382f3f3dd3"></a>Mongolian names traditionally consists of only one personal name.</p>
<div><a name="_typical_name_patterns_11" id="_typical_name_patterns_11"></a><p class="h3Annex">C.31.1 Typical name patterns</p><p class="TableTitle" align="center">Table C.43</p><div align="center"><table style="mso-table-lspace:15.0cm;margin-left:423.0pt;mso-table-rspace:15.0cm;margin-right:423.0pt;mso-table-bspace:14.2pt;mso-table-anchor-vertical:paragraph;mso-table-anchor-horizontal:column;mso-table-overlap:never;" class="MsoISOTable" border="1" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0"><a name="_0147741f-c6de-4591-ac78-b802f6598576" id="_0147741f-c6de-4591-ac78-b802f6598576"></a><tbody><tr><td align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;">given name</td><td align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;">clan name</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<p class="TableTitle" align="center">Table C.44</p><div align="center"><table style="mso-table-lspace:15.0cm;margin-left:423.0pt;mso-table-rspace:15.0cm;margin-right:423.0pt;mso-table-bspace:14.2pt;mso-table-anchor-vertical:paragraph;mso-table-anchor-horizontal:column;mso-table-overlap:never;" class="MsoISOTable" border="1" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0"><a name="_80477992-5dde-456c-ad93-9b14bcd86ab9" id="_80477992-5dde-456c-ad93-9b14bcd86ab9"></a><tbody><tr><td align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;">given name</td><td align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;">family name</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
